    <fr:title text="Typal Binary Relation">Typal Binary Relation</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
    Consider a type <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex>. A <html:strong>typal binary relation</html:strong> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is defined
    to be a family of types <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R(x,y)]]></fr:tex> indexed by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x,y:A]]></fr:tex>.
    <html:ul><html:li><html:strong>Reflexive</html:strong>: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> is reflexive if it comes equipped with
            <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
                \rho :\Pi _{(x:A)}R(x,x)
            ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
        <html:li><html:strong>Symmetric</html:strong>: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> is symmetric if it comes equipped with
            <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
                \sigma :\Pi _{(x,y:A)}R(x,y)\to  R(y,x)
            ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
        <html:li><html:strong>Transitive</html:strong>: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> is transitive if it comes equipped with
            <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
                \tau :\Pi _{(x,y,z:A)}R(x,y)\to  R(y,z)\to  R(x,z)
            ]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul>
    A <html:strong>typal equivalence relation</html:strong> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is a reflexive, symmetric and transitive
    binary relation on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
